          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came in with pain in the lower right side of your tummy. The pain had started around your belly button and moved over 18 hours. You also had nausea, vomiting and no appetite. The team found you had acute appendicitis (inflammation of the appendix)."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team ran some blood tests and a urine test. You also had an ultrasound scan of your tummy. You were given a drip for fluids and an antibiotic (co-amoxiclav) through the drip. You were not allowed to eat or drink at first.\n\nYou then had an operation called a laparoscopic appendicectomy to remove your appendix. During the operation the team found the appendix was inflamed but had not burst. The operation went without problems and blood loss was small. The stitches used will dissolve on their own, so they do not need to be taken out.\n\nA sample from the operation has been sent to the lab. The result is not back yet."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7"
          ],
          "text": "The lab result from your operation is still being processed. You will receive this result when it is ready."
        },
